        "number": 14,
        "title": "Fix language detection to use word-level matching instead of substring matching",
        "body": "Language detection was using substring matching for common words, causing false positives (e.g., \"the\" matching in \"lathe\", \"la\" matching in \"hola\").\n\n## Changes\n\n- Pre-tokenize input text using `re.findall(r\"\\b\\w+\\b\", text_lower)` to extract discrete words\n- Check word membership in the token set instead of substring presence in raw text\n- Added clarifying comment for common endings check (intentionally remains substring-based for suffix detection)\n\n```python\n# Before: substring matching\nif word in text_lower:  # \"the\" matches \"lathe\"\n\n# After: word-level matching  \nwords = set(re.findall(r\"\\b\\w+\\b\", text_lower, flags=re.UNICODE))\nif word in words:  # \"the\" only matches actual \"the\" token\n```\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n\u2728 Let Copilot coding agent [set things up for you](https://github.com/matiasportugau-ui/chatbot-2311/issues/new?title=\u2728+Set+up+Copilot+instructions&body=Configure%20instructions%20for%20this%20repository%20as%20documented%20in%20%5BBest%20practices%20for%20Copilot%20coding%20agent%20in%20your%20repository%5D%28https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips%29%2E%0A%0A%3COnboard%20this%20repo%3E&assignees=copilot) \u2014 coding agent works faster and does higher quality work when set up for your repo.\n",
