        "number": 15,
        "title": "Backup-2025-11-27",
        "body": "- Added WhatsApp conversation ingestion methods (MongoDB, text file, JSON).\n- Updated data ingestion workflow documentation to include WhatsApp.\n- Modified scripts to support WhatsApp data extraction.\n- Added new knowledge file for WhatsApp interactions.\n- Updated timestamps across various JSON files to reflect the latest data.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nEnhance the local chat interface, knowledge ingestion pipeline, and Mercado Libre integration while introducing a centralized language processing module and improved deployment/monitoring tooling.\n\nNew Features:\n- Add a configurable, accessible local HTML chat interface with connection status, settings panel, retry logic, message persistence, browser notifications, and export/import capabilities.\n- Introduce a centralized Python language processing module for intent detection, entity extraction, language identification, caching, and context management.\n- Add Shopify and Mercado Libre ingestion scripts plus a lightweight SQLite store to turn external catalog and Q&A data into consolidated chatbot knowledge.\n- Expose new Mercado Libre dashboards for listings and orders with live data from backend APIs and webhook-driven notifications, plus OAuth and webhook endpoints.\n- Provide an evolved streaming chat experience in the Next.js app using an AI SDK-style interface and backend streaming API.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Extend the dynamic knowledge base loader to auto-discover consolidated knowledge files or fall back to MongoDB, with configuration, validation, and duplicate-safe importing.\n- Improve chatbot behavior by refactoring knowledge import logic into smaller helpers that validate timestamps, deduplicate patterns, and normalize numeric fields.\n- Expand the quotation system product catalog with new insulation materials such as poliestireno and lana de roca.\n- Augment credentials and secure config management to include Mercado Libre settings and expose richer status/diagnostics.\n- Upgrade the dashboard notifications widget to hydrate from stored Mercado Libre webhook events, support filters, and handle read state and error/loading UI.\n- Document repository architecture, language module design, chat interface behavior, monitoring strategy, and improvement roadmap in several new markdown guides.\n\nBuild:\n- Change the npm test script to run the new Mercado Libre integration smoke tests instead of a placeholder.\n\nDeployment:\n- Add environment templates and helper scripts for Vercel/ngrok configuration, full-stack startup, environment setup, and automated knowledge refresh to streamline local and production deployments.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Update README, credentials setup, deployment, data ingestion, chat interface, monitoring, and repository review documentation to reflect the new ingestion pipeline, chat UI, Mercado Libre integration, and operational workflows.\n\nTests:\n- Add a Node-based smoke test script for Mercado Libre endpoints and a Python validator for imported Mercado Libre Q&A knowledge to quickly verify integration health.\n\nChores:\n- Track generated knowledge, raw ingestion artifacts, and validation reports in the repository for easier auditing and debugging.",
