        "number": 5,
        "title": "Remove eval for security",
        "body": "Replaced `eval` with a safe AST-based evaluator for workflow conditions to prevent Remote Code Execution (RCE).\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-9b43f44d-56be-4983-a036-4199588bad29\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/open-in-cursor-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/open-in-cursor-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Open in Cursor\" src=\"https://cursor.com/open-in-cursor.svg\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?id=bc-9b43f44d-56be-4983-a036-4199588bad29\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/open-in-web-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/open-in-web-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Open in Web\" src=\"https://cursor.com/open-in-web.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nReplace unsafe eval-based workflow condition evaluation with a safe, AST-based evaluator to prevent code execution vulnerabilities.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Prevent potential remote code execution by removing use of eval in workflow condition evaluation.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Introduce a dedicated AST-based condition evaluator that supports boolean logic, comparisons, attribute and subscript access, and literal collections for workflow conditions.",
