        "body": "The existing devcontainer only had Python support, but this is a mixed Python/Next.js project requiring both runtimes.\n\n### Changes to `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`\n\n- **Node.js 20** via devcontainer feature for Next.js frontend\n- **Additional VS Code extensions**: ESLint, Tailwind CSS IntelliSense\n- **Editor settings** for JS/TS files using Prettier\n- **Port forwarding**: 3000 (Next.js), 8000 (Python API)\n- **postCreateCommand**: installs both pip and npm dependencies\n\n```json\n\"postCreateCommand\": \"pip install --upgrade pip && ([ -f requirements.txt ] && pip install -r requirements.txt || echo 'No requirements.txt found') && npm install\"\n```\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> Crea codespace para repo\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n\ud83d\udcac We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n",
