        "title": "Add Linux start.sh script and devcontainer for Codespaces support",
        "body": "Adapts `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat` to a Bash script for Linux/Codespaces environments and adds devcontainer configuration.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `start.sh`\n- Detects Python 3.11+ with fallback installation instructions for major distros\n- Runs the same setup sequence as the Windows batch file:\n  - `instalar_dependencias_automatico.py`\n  - `configurar_entorno.py`\n  - `gestionar_servicios.py`\n  - `verificar_sistema_completo.py`\n  - `chat_interactivo.py`\n\n### `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`\n- Python 3.11 base image with Docker-in-Docker for MongoDB container support\n- VS Code extensions: Python, Pylance, Debugpy, Ruff, Prettier\n- Post-create hook installs dependencies from `requirements.txt`\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\n./start.sh\n```\n\nOr open in GitHub Codespaces for a pre-configured environment.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> Adapt the `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat` script into a Bash script (`start.sh`) compatible with Linux environments. This translation aims to make the chatbot project executable in GitHub Codespaces. The new `start.sh` script must:\n> \n> 1. Check if Python 3.11 or higher is installed. If not, instruct the user to install it manually (based on the logic from the `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat` file).\n> 2. Ensure dependencies are installed by running the Python script `instalar_dependencias_automatico.py`.\n> 3. Set up environment variables by invoking the Python script `configurar_entorno.py`.\n> 4. Manage optional services via `gestionar_servicios.py`.\n> 5. Verify the complete system using `verificar_sistema_completo.py`.\n> 6. Finally, launch the chatbot by running `chat_interactivo.py`.\n> \n> Additionally, prepare the repository for GitHub Codespaces by adding the necessary configuration:\n> \n> 1. Create or update the `devcontainer.json` file to include the necessary configurations, such as installing Python 3.11, pip, and other essential dependencies.\n> 2. Include any required extensions or settings for optimal development within the Codespace environment.\n> 3. Ensure the Bash script runs seamlessly in the Codespace while maintaining functionality equivalent to the original `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat`.\n\n\n</details>\n\n*This pull request was created as a result of the following prompt from Copilot chat.*\n> Adapt the `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat` script into a Bash script (`start.sh`) compatible with Linux environments. This translation aims to make the chatbot project executable in GitHub Codespaces. The new `start.sh` script must:\n> \n> 1. Check if Python 3.11 or higher is installed. If not, instruct the user to install it manually (based on the logic from the `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat` file).\n> 2. Ensure dependencies are installed by running the Python script `instalar_dependencias_automatico.py`.\n> 3. Set up environment variables by invoking the Python script `configurar_entorno.py`.\n> 4. Manage optional services via `gestionar_servicios.py`.\n> 5. Verify the complete system using `verificar_sistema_completo.py`.\n> 6. Finally, launch the chatbot by running `chat_interactivo.py`.\n> \n> Additionally, prepare the repository for GitHub Codespaces by adding the necessary configuration:\n> \n> 1. Create or update the `devcontainer.json` file to include the necessary configurations, such as installing Python 3.11, pip, and other essential dependencies.\n> 2. Include any required extensions or settings for optimal development within the Codespace environment.\n> 3. Ensure the Bash script runs seamlessly in the Codespace while maintaining functionality equivalent to the original `INICIAR_CHATBOT.bat`.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 You can make Copilot smarter by setting up custom instructions, customizing its development environment and configuring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. Learn more [Copilot coding agent tips](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips) in the docs.",
