        "title": "[WIP] Setup repository structure and dependencies management",
        "body": "VMC Chatbot Pro Bootstrap Integration Plan\n\nThis PR implements the VMC Chatbot Pro bootstrap script requirements into the Ultimate-CHATBOT monorepo:\n\n**Plan Checklist:**\n- [ ] Update .gitignore with additional exclusions (.dist, .next, .vercel)\n- [ ] Update root package.json with new scripts (evals, dev:web, ci)\n- [ ] Create apps/web Next.js application with Edge runtime API\n- [ ] Create packages/core with orchestrator logic\n- [ ] Create packages/tools with quote_bmc tool\n- [ ] Create packages/rag with graph retrieval\n- [ ] Create packages/guardrails with safety checks\n- [ ] Create promptfoo.yaml for evaluations\n- [ ] Update .github/workflows with promptfoo evals step\n- [ ] Create .env.example with required environment variables\n- [ ] Create vercel.json for edge deployment\n- [ ] Update docker-compose.yml with web service\n- [ ] Update README.md with new information\n- [ ] Create docs/agent_integrador_v5_research.yaml\n- [ ] Create docs/runbook_slo.md\n- [ ] Install dependencies and test build\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# =========================\n# Config editable por t\u00ed\n# =========================\nORG=\"matiasportugau-ui\"\nREPO=\"vmc-chatbot-pro\"\nDEFAULT_BRANCH=\"main\"\nCREATE_PRIVATE=true   # true|false\nUSE_PNPM=true         # si no usas pnpm, cambia a false y el script usar\u00e1 npm\nINIT_WITH_CURSOR_PROMPT=true\n\n# =========================\n# Helpers\n# =========================\npkg() { if $USE_PNPM; then pnpm \"$@\"; else npm \"$@\"; fi; }\npkg_add() { if $USE_PNPM; then pnpm add \"$@\"; else npm install \"$@\"; fi; }\npkg_addD() { if $USE_PNPM; then pnpm add -D \"$@\"; else npm install -D \"$@\"; fi; }\n\n# =========================\n# 0) Crear carpeta y repo\n# =========================\nmkdir -p \"$REPO\"\ncd \"$REPO\"\ngit init -b \"$DEFAULT_BRANCH\"\n\n# Si tienes GitHub CLI, creamos el repo remoto autom\u00e1ticamente\nif command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  VISIBILITY=\"--private\"; $CREATE_PRIVATE || VISIBILITY=\"--public\"\n  gh repo create \"$ORG/$REPO\" $VISIBILITY --source=. --remote=origin --push || true\nelse\n  echo \"\u26a0\ufe0f  No se encontr\u00f3 GitHub CLI (gh). Crea primero el repo https://github.com/$ORG/$REPO y luego:\"\n  echo \"   git remote add origin git@github.com:$ORG/$REPO.git && git push -u origin $DEFAULT_BRANCH\"\nfi\n\n# =========================\n# 1) .gitignore y root setup\n# =========================\ncat > .gitignore <<'EOF'\nnode_modules\n.dist\n.next\n.vercel\n.env\n.env.*\ncoverage\n.DS_Store\nEOF\n\n# =========================\n# 2) package.json (monorepo con workspaces)\n# =========================\ncat > package.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"name\": \"vmc-chatbot-pro\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"workspaces\": [\n    \"apps/*\",\n    \"packages/*\"\n  ],\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"echo Build root OK\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint . --ext .ts,.tsx || true\",\n    \"test\": \"echo Add tests && exit 0\",\n    \"ci\": \"pnpm -r run build && pnpm -r run test\",\n    \"evals\": \"promptfoo eval -c promptfoo.yaml\",\n    \"dev:web\": \"pnpm --filter @vmc/web dev\"\n  }\n}\nEOF\n\n# =========================\n# 3) pnpm o npm, ESLint b\u00e1sico\n# =========================\nif $USE_PNPM; then\n  if ! command -v pnpm >/dev/null 2>&1; then npm i -g pnpm; fi\nfi\npkg_addD eslint\n\n# =========================\n# 4) Estructura carpetas\n# =========================\nmkdir -p apps/web packages/core/src packages/tools packages/rag packages/guardrails infra .github/workflows docs\n\n# =========================\n# 5) App web (placeholder Next.js)\n#     Puedes sustituir luego por create-next-app si prefieres\n# =========================\ncat > apps/web/package.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"name\": \"@vmc/web\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"next dev -p 3000\",\n    \"build\": \"next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start -p 3000\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"next\": \"15.0.0\",\n    \"react\": \"19.0.0-rc-66855b96-20241010\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.0.0-rc-66855b96-20241010\"\n  }\n}\nEOF\n\ncat > apps/web/next.config.js <<'EOF'\n// @ts-check\n/** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\nconst nextConfig = {\n  experimental: { reactCompiler: true }\n};\nmodule.exports = nextConfig;\n\n/* EXPORT_SEAL v1\nproject: vmc-chatbot-pro\nprompt_id: bootstrap-next-config\nversion: 1.0.0\nfile: apps/web/next.config.js\nlang: js\ncreated_at: 2025-11-12T00:00:00Z\nauthor: GPT-5 Thinking\norigin: bootstrap\n*/\nEOF\n\nmkdir -p apps/web/app/(chat)/api/chat\ncat > apps/web/app/page.tsx <<'EOF'\nexport default function Home() {\n  return (\n    <main style={{padding: 24, fontFamily: 'system-ui'}}>\n      <h1>VMC Chatbot Pro</h1>\n      <p>Bienvenido. Esta es la UI m\u00ednima. Integraremos orquestador/RAG/guardrails.</p>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n\n/* EXPORT_SEAL v1\nproject: vmc-chatbot-pro\nprompt_id: bootstrap-home\nversion: 1.0.0\nfile: apps/web/app/page.tsx\nlang: tsx\ncreated_at: 2025-11-12T00:00:00Z\nauthor: GPT-5 Thinking\norigin: bootstrap\n*/\nEOF\n\n# Endpoint minimal para chat (proxy a core)\ncat > apps/web/app/(chat)/api/chat/route.ts <<'EOF'\nimport { NextRequest } from \"next/server\";\nimport { orchestrate } from \"../../../../packages-proxy/orchestrator\";\n\nexport const runtime = \"edge\";\n\nexport async function POST(req: NextRequest) {\n  const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));\n  const res = await orchestrate(body?.message ?? \"\", { trace: true });\n  return new Response(JSON.stringify(res), { status: 200, headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" } });\n}\n\n/* EXPORT_SEAL v1\nproject: vmc-chatbot-pro\nprompt_id: bootstrap-chat-route\nversion: 1.0.0\nfile: apps/web/app/(chat)/api/chat/route.ts\nlang: ts\ncreated_at: 2025-11-12T00:00:00Z\nauthor: GPT-5 Thinking\norigin: bootstrap\n*/\nEOF\n\n# Proxy de import (evita path long):\nmkdir -p apps/web/packages-proxy\ncat > apps/web/packages-proxy/orchestrator.ts <<'EOF'\nexport { orchestrate } from \"../../..//packages/core/src/orchestrator\";\n\n/* EXPORT_SEAL v1\nproject: vmc-chatbot-pro\nprompt_id: proxy-orchestrator\nversion: 1.0.0\nfile: apps/web/packages-proxy/orchestrator.ts\nlang: ts\ncreated_at: 2025-11-12T00:00:00Z\nauthor: GPT-5 Thinking\norigin: bootstrap\n*/\nEOF\n\n# =========================\n# 6) Core Orchestrator (m\u00ednimo funcio...\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 You can make Copilot smarter by setting up custom instructions, customizing its development environment and configuring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. Learn more [Copilot coding agent tips](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips) in the docs.",
