        "title": "Add comprehensive technical documentation suite (6,162 lines)",
        "body": "Created complete technical documentation for Ultimate-CHATBOT system covering architecture, execution flows, components, and operational reference.\n\n## Documentation Structure\n\nFive interconnected documents totaling 6,162 lines (184 KB):\n\n- **TECHNICAL_DOCUMENTATION.md** (355 lines) - Master index with role-based navigation (onboarding, debugging, feature dev, ops)\n- **ARCHITECTURE.md** (1,664 lines) - 6-layer system design: Client \u2192 Orchestration \u2192 NLP \u2192 Service \u2192 Data \u2192 Deployment\n- **LOGIC_FLOW.md** (1,487 lines) - 10+ traced execution paths with timing breakdowns\n- **COMPONENT_STRUCTURE.md** (1,366 lines) - 40+ documented components across Next.js, Rasa, n8n, agents\n- **QUICK_REFERENCE.md** (1,290 lines) - API catalog, database schema, troubleshooting guide\n\n## Key Coverage\n\n**Architecture Layers:**\n- Client: WhatsApp Business API, Chatwoot, Next.js dashboard\n- Orchestration: n8n workflows (4 documented), Event Bus, 4 background agents\n- NLP: Rasa 3.6 (15+ intents, 10+ entities, custom actions)\n- Service: Quote engine, context manager (8K token window), vector RAG\n- Data: Postgres (11 tables), Qdrant (semantic search), Redis (cache/sessions)\n\n**Execution Flows:**\n- Complete message trace: WhatsApp \u2192 Chatwoot \u2192 n8n \u2192 Rasa \u2192 Services (12 steps, ~800ms avg)\n- Quotation generation with price matrix and tier calculations\n- Context compression at 80% token usage (6,400/8,000)\n- Vector search with embedding generation and reranking\n\n**Components:**\n```typescript\n// Example: Context management structure documented\ninterface ConversationContext {\n  sessionId: string\n  messages: Message[]\n  tokenCount: number        // Tracked against 8K limit\n  summary?: string          // Generated at compression\n  compressionCount: number  // Compression cycle tracker\n}\n```\n\n**API Reference:**\n- 8+ REST endpoints with curl examples\n- Rasa webhook integration patterns\n- n8n workflow trigger mechanisms\n- Qdrant vector search queries\n\n## Navigation Aids\n\nCross-referenced by:\n- Developer role (new hire path, debugging traces, feature patterns)\n- Technology stack (frontend/backend/data layer jumps)\n- Use case (adding intents, building features, debugging flows)\n\nExample learning path: Master index \u2192 Architecture overview \u2192 Service layer \u2192 API catalog \u2192 Build first feature.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>Extracted comprehensive technical documentation for the Chat SDK chatbot, covering system architecture, execution flows, and component structure.</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>Extracted comprehensive technical documentation for the Chat SDK chatbot, covering system architecture, execution flows, and component structure.\n> \n> ## Documentation Structure (3,240+ lines, 83 KB)\n> \n> **TECHNICAL_DOCUMENTATION.md** - Master index\n> - Documentation map by role (onboarding, debugging, feature dev, ops)\n> - System overview and feature matrix\n> - Quick navigation to relevant sections\n> \n> **ARCHITECTURE.md** - System design\n> - 6 layers: Frontend (React/Next.js), API (Routes/Actions), AI (SDK/Tools), Data (Postgres/Drizzle), Auth (NextAuth/JWT), Deployment (Vercel)\n> - Design patterns: Server Components, Streaming SSE, Tool Calling, Optimistic Updates\n> - Security: JWT sessions, rate limiting, input validation\n> \n> **LOGIC_FLOW.md** - Execution traces\n> - 10+ step-by-step flows: auth (guest auto-creation, registration), chat (client \u2192 API \u2192 AI \u2192 stream), tool execution, artifact CRUD\n> - Streaming mechanics: SSE transport, smooth word-level chunking, resumable streams\n> - Error handling with custom ChatSDKError types\n> \n> **COMPONENT_STRUCTURE.md** - UI architecture\n> - Component tree: Chat \u2192 Messages \u2192 Message \u2192 MultimodalInput \u2192 Artifact\n> - 40+ components with props/state/hooks\n> - Editors: ProseMirror (text), CodeMirror (code), react-data-grid (sheets)\n> - State: useChat hook, SWR caching, Context providers\n> \n> **QUICK_REFERENCE.md** - Developer lookup\n> - API catalog: 8 REST endpoints, 4 server actions\n> - DB schema: 7 tables with relationships\n> - Environment setup, NPM scripts, troubleshooting\n> \n> ## Coverage\n> \n> - Complete data flow: User input \u2192 Auth/Rate limit \u2192 AI streaming \u2192 Tool execution \u2192 DB persistence\n> - AI integration: xAI Grok models (Vision, Reasoning), 4 tools (weather, createDocument, updateDocument, requestSuggestions)\n> - Authentication: Middleware-based, guest auto-creation, JWT cookies, bcrypt hashing\n> - Artifacts: Real-time streaming content generation, 4 types (text/code/sheet/image), nested AI calls\n> \n> Organized for multiple use cases: onboarding paths, debugging traces, code patterns, deployment configs.\n> \n> <!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> \n> <summary>Original prompt</summary>\n> \n> > Extract logic and architecture of this chat bot and tb\n> \n> \n> </details>\n> \n> \n> \n> <!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n> ---\n> \n> \ud83d\udcac We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n> \n> \n> _Publicaci\u00f3n original de @Copilot en https://github.com/matiasportugau-ui/nextjs-ai-chatbot2/pull/1_</issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n- Fixes matiasportugau-ui/Ultimate-CHATBOT#3\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n\ud83d\udcac We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n",
